course: dictionary
lesson: 5700
title: Logos and brands
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A logo is a small picture, symbol or special design that a company, team, school or group uses so people recognise it. Think of the shape on a football shirt or a shop sign: you know whose it is before you read a single word. «The Nike swoosh was designed in 1971 by a design student, Carolyn Davidson.» The logo is a symbol, not the whole company.
explain: A logo helps people remember a brand. «The logo became valuable because of the brand built around it.» On its own a logo is just a picture. It gains its meaning from the business, the products and the trust people put in them.
explain: Because logos are easy to copy, they can also be used to trick people. «Scammers copy real logos, pretend to be banks, parcel companies, the government...» A logo alone never proves that something is real. Check the real website, not the screenshot.
fact: A logo is a small picture, symbol or special design.
fact: «Logo» means a symbol that helps people recognise a company, team, school or group.
fact: Clubs, classes and schools can have logos too, and you can design one yourself.
fact: «Logos» is the plural of «logo».
fact: A logo can be copied, so seeing one does not prove that a message is true.
exercise: What is a logo? | A long story that a company tells | A loud sound made by a team | *A small picture, symbol or special design that a group uses so people recognise it | A kind of football boot
exercise: «The Nike swoosh was designed in 1971 by a design student, Carolyn Davidson.» Who designed the Nike swoosh? | Nike | Carolyn's dog | *Carolyn Davidson | A football club
exercise: Why might a company design a logo? | *So people will recognise it | So it can be eaten | So it weighs more | So it can hide from people
test: «Likes, shares and a copied logo do not make a story true.» What does this tell you about logos? | Logos only appear on food packets | A logo proves a story is real | Every logo is made by a bank | *A logo can be copied, so it does not prove a story is true
test: The sentence says to find the real article «on the outlet's own website». Why? | *Because a screenshot is easy to change | To see the page colours | Because websites are always fake | To get free likes
exam: Which statement about logos is true? | Any logo proves a company is honest | Logos only appear on school bags | *A logo is a symbol that helps people recognise a company, team, school or group | A logo is a long written story
